  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with multiple potassium channel subunits, specifically Kcnc3, Kcna7, and Kcnv1, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcna6, suggesting a potential role for Guanidine in modulating the function of delayed rectifier potassium channels. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable interaction, with Guanidine likely acting as a modulator of these channels. The mechanism appears to involve Guanidine binding to these channels, which in turn affects the activity of Kcna6, potentially influencing cellular potassium homeostasis. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic link between Guanidine and Kcna6, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise functional role of this interaction.",
